  "id": "DrugBank_DB15598 - MONDO_grouped_1357_387",
  "verbalization": "Ferric Maltol is associated with Hypochromic Anemia through a chain of indications that link it to Iron Deficiency Anemia and Ferric Oxide, which in turn is linked to Hypochromic Anemia. This suggests that Ferric Maltol may act as a mediator in the pathophysiology of Hypochromic Anemia, potentially by influencing iron metabolism. The evidence from the three paths highlights a consistent mechanism where Ferric Maltol is linked to Iron Deficiency Anemia, which is then connected to Ferric Oxide and finally to Hypochromic Anemia. The overlapping pathways and similar scores across the paths support a unified explanation, emphasizing the role of Ferric Oxide in the chain of events leading to Hypochromic Anemia. The integration of these pathways suggests that Ferric Maltol may influence iron availability or utilization, thereby contributing to the development of Hypochromic Anemia.",
